  "term": "Serax",
  "definition": "Serax is oxazepam, a synthetic benzodiazepine derivative with anxiety-reducing and sedative-hypnotic effects. Its exact action is not fully established, but it appears to increase GABA receptor affinity for GABA and extend GABA’s effects at synapses.",
